[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Delegated Properties and DSL Construction in Android (Kotlin)"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Kotlin provides powerful features like delegated properties and type-safe builders that allow developers to construct clean, highly readable Domain Specific Languages (DSLs). In Android development, these concepts simplify complex UI hierarchies, layout configurations, and state management."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Property Delegation in Kotlin"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Property delegation allows you to hand off the getter and setter responsibilities of a property to another helper object. Instead of implementing the logic manually every time, you use the 'by' keyword."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"class PreferenceDelegate<T>(private val key: String, private val defaultValue: T) {
    operator fun getValue(thisRef: Any?, property: KProperty<*>): T {
        // Retrieve from SharedPreferences
        return defaultValue
    }
    operator fun setValue(thisRef: Any?, property: KProperty<*>, value: T) {
        // Save to SharedPreferences
    }
}"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Building a Type-Safe UI DSL for Android"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"By leveraging Kotlin lambdas with receivers, we can build custom DSLs to construct Android layouts or configuration objects cleanly without XML."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"class LayoutBuilder {
    val views = mutableListOf<String>()

    fun textView(init: TextViewBuilder.() -> Unit) {
        val tv = TextViewBuilder().apply(init)
        views.add(tv.build())
    }
}

class TextViewBuilder {
    var text: String = ""
    var textSize: Float = 14f

    fun build(): String {
        return "TextView(text=\"$text\", size=$textSize)"
    }
}

fun layout(init: LayoutBuilder.() -> Unit): LayoutBuilder {
    return LayoutBuilder().apply(init)
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Combining Delegates and DSLs"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can combine custom delegated properties inside your DSL builders to handle validation, automatic change notifications, or state binding effortlessly."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use 'getValue' and 'setValue' operator functions to create custom delegates."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Apply '@DslMarker' annotations to restrict scope and prevent improper nesting in complex builders."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Leverage lambdas with receivers (e.g., 'Builder.() -> Unit') for intuitive DSL syntax."}]
